{"type":"npc","name":"Amutu","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":28,"temp":0,"max":28,"details":""},"ac":{"value":17,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":25}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"death-effects","exceptions":[]},{"type":"disease","exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"poison","value":4,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]},{"type":"void","value":4,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["chthonian","common","diabolic","empyrean","requian"],"details":""},"level":{"value":2},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Of all the known varieties of psychopomp, amutu are among the most likely to interact with and the living and try to assist them in matters other than dealing with undead or other enemies of Purgatory. They have been tasked by their superiors, following the chain all the way up to psychopomp ushers and the deities of Purgatory, to manage deaths caused by resource scarcity, such as starvation, dehydration, or exposure to the elements. They travel far and wide through the mortal realm, offering warnings and advice against such catastrophes. When prevention is impossible, they help guide the souls of the departed to the afterlife, lest they linger behind and haunt their former homes or rise again to devour the living. Amutu have also been known to help with childbirth when an unfortunate mother is caught far from civilization and to teach new lovers about herbal contraceptives.</p><p>An amutu stands about as tall as a halfling, with a light coppery complexion and the feet and head of an owl or other bird of prey. They favor traveling in arid regions and typically wear light, non-restrictive clothing. Like many psychopomps, amutu wear masks. They favor brightly painted wooden masks, often carved with exaggerated humanoid features and ringed with feathers. These feathers are a mixture of their own creations and gifts they have received from friends and allies.</p><p>Though amutu are supernatural beings, they recognize that most disasters are made worse not by magical interference but by the corrupting forces of greed. Thus, their foes include people who hoard resources while others struggle to meet their basic needs, as well as those who deliberately build shoddy infrastructure to save money, leaving communities vulnerable to accidents and natural disasters. They also oppose more fantastical threats, such as gremlins, ghouls, and priests of famine deities (such as Havath in the world of Alacar). When more powerful menaces like daemons or sahkils emerge, amutu seek the aid of heroes to prevent tragedy.</p><h2>Parliament of Owls</h2><p>Folklore concerning the wisdom of owls might have its origin in the activities of amutus. Tales in which owls provide advice or gather together in groups to consult about supernatural events probably refer to the counsels of amutus. Although this tale might be true, amutus fervently deny having anything to do with other folk tales, such as the one in which malevolent owls pass judgment on mortals who break the most minor of rules, pursuing them, and then tearing them to pieces.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 5/12/22 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (slashing), armor (light), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Crafting, Lore [Midwifery], Nature, Religion, Society, Stealth)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, constitution, death, dexterity, energy resistant (vitality, void), life, lifeward armor, light, mind, mind shield, sensory (darkvision), spells (Divine: @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.Mt6ZzkVX8Q4xigFq]{Create Food}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.WzLKjSw6hsBhuklC]{Create Water}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.XXqE1eY3w3z6xJCB]{Invisibility}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.WBmvzNDfpwka3qT4]{Light}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.8xRzLhwGL7Dgy3EZ]{Sanctuary}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.SnjhtQYexDtNDdEg]{Stabilize}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.yV7Ouzaoe7DHLESI]{Ventriloquism}), water, wild, winged, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Aleander Macleod","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":2},"dex":{"mod":4},"con":{"mod":3},"int":{"mod":1},"wis":{"mod":4},"cha":{"mod":2}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":10,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"lifesense","acuity":"imprecise","range":60}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":7,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":10,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":8,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":8},"athletics":{"base":6},"crafting":{"base":7},"nature":{"base":8},"religion":{"base":8},"society":{"base":7},"stealth":{"base":8}},"traits":{"value":["monitor","psychopomp"],"rarity":"common","size":{"value":"sm"}}},"_id":"KemOBoo7qirkvu0B","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/amutu.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Amutu","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/amutu.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1.6,"scaleY":1.6,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuatio